# link_pack -- packer -> unpacker round trip: same words, order and fields; flit parity and size; CRC flush; progress
# BW = 16, WPF = 32, XW = YW = 3 (the silicon links), the drop 0.42 packer with both sides registered (the beat in an input
# register, the link flit in an output register): the beats out carry the words accepted, in order, none invented or
# repeated, with their type / tag / head / stream fields and PSUM columns; every link flit even parity and 1..WPF words,
# every beat out even parity and 1..BW words; a CRC (any one-word type) taken from the input register leaves only itself
# in flight besides the beat behind it; with the sink ready no beat waits more than 2 cycles (the bound of the
# combinational packer: the registers add no cycle to it). Full proof by k-induction with invariants over the input
# register, the output register, the pending flit and a ghost of its prefix word parities; link_pack_fv.sv holds the
# harness. Two tasks (drop 0.42; one took 788 s in the sandbox, above the job's 600 s per task), each a full proof of
# its group of properties with the structural invariants: stream (the round trip, the counts in flight, the sizes, the
# CRC flush, the wait bound) and parity (the parity of every link flit and beat out, the running-parity invariants).
# The engine is bitwuzla: the running parity's induction step (word parities through the merge's barrel shift) does not
# close with yices in 540 s; for the stream group bitwuzla took 323 s, yices 690 s.
[tasks]
stream
parity

[options]
mode prove
depth 2

[engines]
smtbmc bitwuzla

[script]
plugin -i slang
stream: read_slang -DFORMAL -DLP_NO_PARITY --top link_pack_fv link_pack.sv link_pack_fv.sv
parity: read_slang -DFORMAL -DLP_NO_STREAM --top link_pack_fv link_pack.sv link_pack_fv.sv
prep -top link_pack_fv

[files]
rtl/link_pack.sv
formal/link_pack_fv.sv
